{"name": "host-from-prose", "why": "the plainest case: an IP in a sentence becomes a Host", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": false, "input": "Got a shell on web01 (10.10.10.5) through the nginx box.\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "host", "fields": [{"name": "ip", "value": "10.10.10.5", "evidence": "10.10.10.5"}, {"name": "hostnames", "value": "web01", "evidence": "web01"}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [{"type": "host", "id": "host:10.10.10.5", "ip": "10.10.10.5", "hostnames": ["web01"]}], "notices": []}}
{"name": "host-and-service", "why": "a port mentioned next to a host becomes a Service on it", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": false, "input": "Outdated Jetty on dc01:8080/tcp is probably the better path.\ndc01 is 10.10.10.6.\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "host", "fields": [{"name": "ip", "value": "10.10.10.6", "evidence": "10.10.10.6"}, {"name": "hostnames", "value": "dc01", "evidence": "dc01"}]}, {"type": "service", "fields": [{"name": "host", "value": "10.10.10.6", "evidence": "10.10.10.6"}, {"name": "port", "value": "8080", "evidence": "8080"}, {"name": "protocol", "value": "tcp", "evidence": "tcp"}, {"name": "product", "value": "Jetty", "evidence": "Jetty"}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [{"type": "host", "id": "host:10.10.10.6"}, {"type": "service", "id": "service:10.10.10.6-tcp-8080", "port": 8080, "product": "Jetty"}], "notices": []}}
{"name": "service-without-a-protocol", "why": "Trove does not assume tcp — a defaulted key field is an uncited claim", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": false, "input": "dc01 (10.10.10.6) has something on 8080.\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "host", "fields": [{"name": "ip", "value": "10.10.10.6", "evidence": "10.10.10.6"}]}, {"type": "service", "fields": [{"name": "host", "value": "10.10.10.6", "evidence": "10.10.10.6"}, {"name": "port", "value": "8080", "evidence": "8080"}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [{"type": "host", "id": "host:10.10.10.6"}], "notices": ["did not say tcp or udp"]}}
{"name": "service-by-hostname", "why": "a service may name its host by a hostname proposed in the same input", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": false, "input": "dc01 (10.10.10.6) is running SMB on 445/tcp.\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "host", "fields": [{"name": "ip", "value": "10.10.10.6", "evidence": "10.10.10.6"}, {"name": "hostnames", "value": "dc01", "evidence": "dc01"}]}, {"type": "service", "fields": [{"name": "host", "value": "dc01", "evidence": "dc01"}, {"name": "port", "value": "445", "evidence": "445"}, {"name": "protocol", "value": "tcp", "evidence": "SMB on 445/tcp"}, {"name": "name", "value": "SMB", "evidence": "SMB"}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [{"type": "host", "id": "host:10.10.10.6"}, {"type": "service", "id": "service:10.10.10.6-tcp-445", "port": 445, "name": "SMB"}], "notices": []}}
{"name": "credential-from-prose", "why": "loot written down in a sentence is still loot", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": false, "input": "svc_backup creds work over SMB on 10.10.10.6. Password is Winter2024!\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "credential", "fields": [{"name": "principal", "value": "svc_backup", "evidence": "svc_backup"}, {"name": "secret", "value": "Winter2024!", "evidence": "Winter2024!"}, {"name": "state", "value": "validated", "evidence": "creds work over SMB"}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [{"type": "credential", "principal": "svc_backup", "secret": "Winter2024!", "state": "validated"}], "notices": []}}
{"name": "credential-hash", "why": "a hash pasted into a note, with the type the author named", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": false, "input": "Pulled the NTLM hash for admin: 31d6cfe0d16ae931b73c59d7e0c089c0\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "credential", "fields": [{"name": "principal", "value": "admin", "evidence": "admin"}, {"name": "secret_hash", "value": "31d6cfe0d16ae931b73c59d7e0c089c0", "evidence": "31d6cfe0d16ae931b73c59d7e0c089c0"}, {"name": "hash_type", "value": "ntlm", "evidence": "NTLM"}, {"name": "state", "value": "found", "evidence": "Pulled the NTLM hash"}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [{"type": "credential", "principal": "admin", "hash_type": "ntlm", "secret_hash": "31d6cfe0d16ae931b73c59d7e0c089c0"}], "notices": []}}
{"name": "finding-with-host", "why": "a finding the operator described, attached to a host they named", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": false, "input": "10.10.10.5 allows anonymous FTP. Anyone can list /pub.\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "host", "fields": [{"name": "ip", "value": "10.10.10.5", "evidence": "10.10.10.5"}]}, {"type": "finding", "fields": [{"name": "title", "value": "Anonymous FTP allowed", "evidence": "allows anonymous FTP"}, {"name": "host", "value": "10.10.10.5", "evidence": "10.10.10.5"}, {"name": "description", "value": "Anyone can list /pub.", "evidence": "Anyone can list /pub."}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [{"type": "host", "id": "host:10.10.10.5"}, {"type": "finding", "title": "Anonymous FTP allowed", "host_id": "host:10.10.10.5", "severity": null}], "notices": []}}
{"name": "note-kept-as-note", "why": "an intention is not a record — it is a note", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": false, "input": "Still need to check whether 10.10.10.6 is the only DC. Client said two.\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "note", "fields": [{"name": "text", "value": "Still need to check whether 10.10.10.6 is the only DC.", "evidence": "Still need to check whether 10.10.10.6 is the only DC."}, {"name": "tags", "value": "todo", "evidence": "Still need to check"}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [{"type": "note", "text": "Still need to check whether 10.10.10.6 is the only DC.", "tags": ["todo"]}], "notices": []}}
{"name": "empty-is-an-answer", "why": "an input with nothing in it yields nothing, and that is correct", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": false, "input": "Coffee run. Back in ten.\n", "response": {"records": []}, "expect": {"records": [], "notices": []}}
{"name": "multi-record-note", "why": "the real fixture: several records out of one operator note", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": false, "input": "Day 2 notes\n\nGot a shell on web01 (10.10.10.5).\n\nsvc_backup creds work over SMB on 10.10.10.6.\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "host", "fields": [{"name": "ip", "value": "10.10.10.5", "evidence": "10.10.10.5"}, {"name": "hostnames", "value": "web01", "evidence": "web01"}]}, {"type": "host", "fields": [{"name": "ip", "value": "10.10.10.6", "evidence": "10.10.10.6"}]}, {"type": "credential", "fields": [{"name": "principal", "value": "svc_backup", "evidence": "svc_backup"}, {"name": "state", "value": "validated", "evidence": "creds work over SMB"}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [{"type": "host", "id": "host:10.10.10.5"}, {"type": "host", "id": "host:10.10.10.6"}, {"type": "credential", "principal": "svc_backup"}], "notices": []}}
{"name": "tool-output-kind", "why": "output from a tool with no parser: hosts and services, never notes", "source": "nikto-out.log", "kind": "tool-output", "unconstrained": false, "input": "Nikto scan report for 10.10.10.5\n+ Server: Apache/2.4.49\n+ Port 80/tcp open\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "host", "fields": [{"name": "ip", "value": "10.10.10.5", "evidence": "10.10.10.5"}]}, {"type": "service", "fields": [{"name": "host", "value": "10.10.10.5", "evidence": "10.10.10.5"}, {"name": "port", "value": "80", "evidence": "80"}, {"name": "protocol", "value": "tcp", "evidence": "tcp"}, {"name": "product", "value": "Apache/2.4.49", "evidence": "Apache/2.4.49"}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [{"type": "host", "id": "host:10.10.10.5"}, {"type": "service", "id": "service:10.10.10.5-tcp-80", "port": 80}], "notices": []}}
{"name": "invented-evidence", "why": "schema-valid and WRONG: the span is not in the input", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": false, "input": "Got a shell on web01 (10.10.10.5).\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "host", "fields": [{"name": "ip", "value": "10.10.10.5", "evidence": "10.10.10.5"}, {"name": "os", "value": "Windows Server 2019", "evidence": "running Windows Server 2019"}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [{"type": "host", "id": "host:10.10.10.5", "os": null}], "notices": ["does not appear in"]}}
{"name": "paraphrased-evidence", "why": "close is not quoted: a reworded span is still not the bytes", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": false, "input": "The FTP service lets anyone in without a password.\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "finding", "fields": [{"name": "title", "value": "Anonymous FTP", "evidence": "FTP allows anonymous access"}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [], "notices": ["does not appear in"]}}
{"name": "severity-refused", "why": "severity is the operator's, never the model's", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": true, "input": "10.10.10.5 allows anonymous FTP.\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "finding", "fields": [{"name": "title", "value": "Anonymous FTP allowed", "evidence": "allows anonymous FTP"}, {"name": "severity", "value": "high", "evidence": "allows anonymous FTP"}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [{"type": "finding", "title": "Anonymous FTP allowed", "severity": null}], "notices": ["operator's"]}}
{"name": "port-not-a-number", "why": "a port that is not a number is not a port", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": false, "input": "Jetty is on the admin/tcp port of 10.10.10.6.\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "host", "fields": [{"name": "ip", "value": "10.10.10.6", "evidence": "10.10.10.6"}]}, {"type": "service", "fields": [{"name": "host", "value": "10.10.10.6", "evidence": "10.10.10.6"}, {"name": "protocol", "value": "tcp", "evidence": "tcp"}, {"name": "port", "value": "admin", "evidence": "admin/tcp port"}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [{"type": "host", "id": "host:10.10.10.6"}], "notices": ["not a port number", "not a usable record"]}}
{"name": "unknown-field", "why": "a field the schema does not offer is ignored, not stuffed into ext", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": true, "input": "web01 is 10.10.10.5.\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "host", "fields": [{"name": "ip", "value": "10.10.10.5", "evidence": "10.10.10.5"}, {"name": "confidence", "value": "0.9", "evidence": "web01"}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [{"type": "host", "id": "host:10.10.10.5"}], "notices": ["unknown field"]}}
{"name": "unknown-type", "why": "a record type the model made up is ignored", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": true, "input": "web01 is 10.10.10.5.\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "vulnerability", "fields": [{"name": "ip", "value": "10.10.10.5", "evidence": "10.10.10.5"}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [], "notices": ["unknown record type"]}}
{"name": "unresolvable-host", "why": "a service on a host nobody has heard of is dropped, not guessed at", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": false, "input": "Something is listening on 8080/tcp somewhere.\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "service", "fields": [{"name": "host", "value": "somewhere", "evidence": "somewhere"}, {"name": "protocol", "value": "tcp", "evidence": "tcp"}, {"name": "port", "value": "8080", "evidence": "8080"}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [], "notices": ["no host in this engagement answers to it", "not a usable record"]}}
{"name": "service-named-by-name", "why": "a finding may not name a service by name — edges are the core's job", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": false, "input": "The Jetty console on 10.10.10.6 has no lockout.\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "host", "fields": [{"name": "ip", "value": "10.10.10.6", "evidence": "10.10.10.6"}]}, {"type": "finding", "fields": [{"name": "title", "value": "No account lockout", "evidence": "has no lockout"}, {"name": "host", "value": "10.10.10.6", "evidence": "10.10.10.6"}, {"name": "service", "value": "Jetty console", "evidence": "Jetty console"}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [{"type": "host", "id": "host:10.10.10.6"}, {"type": "finding", "title": "No account lockout", "service_id": null}], "notices": ["services are linked by the deterministic layer"]}}
{"name": "no-key-field", "why": "a record with no identifying field is not a record", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": false, "input": "Something odd about that box.\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "host", "fields": [{"name": "os", "value": "Linux", "evidence": "Something odd"}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [], "notices": ["not a usable record"]}}
{"name": "empty-value-skipped", "why": "an empty value is not a claim", "source": "note.md", "kind": null, "unconstrained": false, "input": "web01 is 10.10.10.5.\n", "response": {"records": [{"type": "host", "fields": [{"name": "ip", "value": "10.10.10.5", "evidence": "10.10.10.5"}, {"name": "os", "value": "", "evidence": "web01"}]}]}, "expect": {"records": [{"type": "host", "id": "host:10.10.10.5", "os": null}], "notices": []}}
